_01R4qp2Au9aae3ySuyDMjJXv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build fails because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py::round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses ROUND_HALF_EVEN.\n\n**Change:** `round_money` now uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` instead of `ROUND_HALF_UP`.\n\n- `2.675` -> `2.68` (unchanged)\n- `2.665` -> `2.66` (was `2.67`)\n\n**CI:** run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.\n\nNote: this changes how exact half-cent amounts are rounded for every caller of `round_money`.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so the PR may or may not have been created. I'll check before retrying so I don't open a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01WmwN12UAQ1qVAvDR1HPYhm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "open", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR (#101) was created despite the timeout, but alex isn't listed as a reviewer. I'll add him to that PR rather than open a new one.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_019qxrPfFQ9ZVXNqAa9D3VDk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own description says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`), as the test expects. I couldn't look up FIN-212 because it isn't in the advisory system, but the code's description and the test agree on what's wrong.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Now 2.665 rounds to 2.66 instead of 2.67, and 2.675 still rounds to 2.68.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on the fix.\n- **PR:** The request to open the PR timed out but went through anyway. I checked the open PRs before retrying to avoid a duplicate, and found #101 with no reviewers on it. I added alex to that PR.\n\nI haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval. The PR description also notes that this changes how amounts ending in exactly half a cent are rounded for everything that calls `round_money`.", "type": "text"}]}]}